# UI / UX Design

- Mobile-first Tailwind. Layouts must work on phone, tablet, and desktop dashboards.
- Professional restaurant-ops look: clear hierarchy, dense but readable tables, obvious primary actions.
- Every list/table needs loading, empty, and error states.
- Forms: labeled inputs, inline validation messages, disabled submit while pending.
- Modals/drawers must be keyboard-usable and closable; icon-only buttons need `aria-label`.
- Do not hide destructive actions (void bill, cancel reservation) behind unconfirmed clicks.
- Use Recharts only on analytics views, with a non-chart fallback when data is empty.
- Prefer shared primitives (`Button`, `Card`, `DataTable`, `PageHeader`) over one-off styles.

```javascript
// ✅ GOOD — empty state, not a blank table
if (!orders.length) {
  return <p className="text-sm text-slate-500">No open orders.</p>;
}
```
